[VINCENT]
I need a big fat magic marker, any felt pen'll do, but a magic marker would be great.
ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງການເຄື່ອງຫມາຍຊະຍາກອນທີ່ຫນາແຫນ້ນ, ກະທູ້ felt
ໃດກໍ່ຈະເຮັດໄດ້, ແຕ່ເຄື່ອງ ຫມາຍ magic ຈະດີເລີດ.

519
00:33:06,100 --> 00:33:08,100
[JODY]
Hold on.
ລໍຖ້າ.

520
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:11,400
[LANCE]
It's ready, I'll tell you what to do.
ມັນພ້ອມແລ້ວ, ຂ້ອຍຈະບອກເຈົ້າວ່າຕ້ອງເຮັດແນວໃດ.

521
00:33:11,900 --> 00:33:14,000
[VINCENT]
You're gonna give her the shot.
ເຈົ້າຈະສັກຢາໃຫ້ນາງ.

522
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:16,950
[LANCE]
No, you're gonna give her the shot.
ບໍ່, ເຈົ້າຈະໃຫ້ນາງສັກຢາ.

523
00:33:17,450 --> 00:33:19,450
[VINCENT]
I've never does this before.
ຂ້ອຍບໍ່ເຄີຍເຮັດແບບນີ້ກ່ອນ.

524
00:33:19,950 --> 00:33:25,950
[LANCE]
I've never done this before either, and I ain't starting now. You brought 'er here, that means you give her the shot. The day I bring an ODing bitch to your place, then I gotta give her the shot.
ຂ້ອຍບໍ່ເຄີຍເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ກ່ອນເຊັ່ນກັນ, ແລະຂ້ອຍຈະບໍ່ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນດຽວນີ້. ເຈົ້າເອົານາງມາບ່ອນນີ້, ນັ້ນ ຫມາຍ
ຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າໃຫ້ນາງສັກຢາ. ມື້ທີ່ຂ້ອຍເອົາໂຊກແຊວ ODing ມາເຮືອນຂອງທ່ານ, ຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງໃຫ້ນາງສູບຢາ.

525
00:33:26,450 --> 00:33:28,450
[JODY]
Got it.
ຂ້ອຍເຂົ້າໃຈແລ້ວ.

526
00:33:28,950 --> 00:33:30,950
[VINCENT]
Okay, what do I do?
ດີແລ້ວ, ຂ້ອຍຈະເຮັດແນວໃດ?

527
00:33:31,450 --> 00:33:37,450
[LANCE]
Well, you're giving her an injection of adrenaline straight to her heart. But she's got a breast plate in front of her heart, so you gotta pierce through that. So what you gotta do is bring the needle down in a stabbing motion.
ດີ, ເຈົ້າ ກໍາ ລັງສັກຢາແອດຣີນາລິນໃຫ້ນາງໂດຍກົງສູ່ຫົວໃຈຂອງນາງ. ແຕ່ນາງມີແຜ່ນທ້ອງຢູ່ຕໍ່ຫນ້າຫົວໃຈຂອງລາວ,
ສະນັ້ນເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເຈາະຜ່ານນັ້ນ. ສະນັ້ນສິ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເຮັດແມ່ນເອົາກະດານລົງໃນການເຄື່ອນໄຫວ stabling ໄດ້.

528
00:33:37,950 --> 00:33:39,950
[VINCENT]
I gotta stab her?
ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງດອກນາງບໍ?

529
00:33:40,450 --> 00:33:46,050
[LANCE]
If you want the needle to pierce through to her heart, you gotta stab her hard.
ຖ້າເຈົ້າຢາກໃຫ້ເຂັມເຈາະຜ່ານຫົວໃຈຂອງນາງ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງດອກນາງຢ່າງແຂງແຮງ.

530
00:33:46,550 --> 00:33:48,550
[VINCENT]
What happens after that?
ຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນ?

531
00:33:49,050 --> 00:33:51,050
[LANCE]
I'm curious about that myself.
ຂ້ອຍຢາກຮູ້ສຶກກ່ຽວກັບເລື່ອງນັ້ນເອງ.

532
00:33:51,550 --> 00:33:53,650
[VINCENT]
This ain't a fuckin' joke man!
ນີ້ແມ່ນບໍ່ແມ່ນຄົນຢອກຊື່ໆ!

533
00:33:54,150 --> 00:33:58,000
[LANCE]
She's supposed to come out of it like �  � that.
ນາງຄວນຈະອອກຈາກມັນແບບນັ້ນ.

534
00:33:58,500 --> 00:34:00,500
[VINCENT]
Count to three.
ນັບຈົນຮອດສາມ.

535
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,000
[LANCE]
One...
ຫນຶ່ງ...

536
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:05,500
[LANCE]
...two...
ສອງ...

537
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,000
[LANCE]
...three!
ສາມ!

538
00:34:08,500 --> 00:34:10,500
[LANCE]
If you're okay, say something.
ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ເປັນຫຍັງ, ເວົ້າບາງສິ່ງບາງຢ່າງ.

539
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:13,000
[MIA]
Something.
ບາງຢ່າງ.

540
00:34:13,500 --> 00:34:15,500
[JODY]
Anybody want a beer?
ມີໃຜຢາກເບຍບໍ?

541
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,000
[VINCENT]
Mia!
ມິຍ!

542
00:34:18,500 --> 00:34:21,650
[VINCENT]
What are your thoughts on how to handle this?
ເຈົ້າຄິດແນວໃດກ່ຽວກັບວິທີຮັບມືກັບເລື່ອງນີ້?

543
00:34:22,150 --> 00:34:24,150
[MIA]
What's yours?
ຂອງເຈົ້າແມ່ນຫຍັງ?

544
00:34:24,650 --> 00:34:30,650
[VINCENT]
Well I'm of the opinion that Marsellus can live his whole live and never ever hear of this incident.
ດີຂ້ອຍມີຄວາມຄິດເຫັນວ່າ
ມາເຊລັສສາມາດດໍາລົງຊີວິດຕະຫຼອດຊີວິດຂອງລາວແລະບໍ່ເຄີຍໄດ້ຍິນກ່ຽວກັບເຫດການນີ້ເລີຍ.

545
00:34:31,150 --> 00:34:37,150
[MIA]
Don't worry about it. If Marsellus ever heard of this, I'd be in as much trouble as you.
ຢ່າກັງວົນກ່ຽວກັບມັນ. ຖ້າມາເຊລັສເຄີຍໄດ້ຍິນເລື່ອງນີ້
, ຂ້ອຍຈະຢູ່ໃນຄວາມຫຍຸ້ງຍາກເທົ່າກັບເຈົ້າ.

546
00:34:37,650 --> 00:34:39,650
[VINCENT]
I seriously doubt that.
ຂ້ອຍສົງໄສຢ່າງຈິງໃຈວ່າ.

547
00:34:40,150 --> 00:34:43,300
[MIA]
If you can keep a secret, so can I.
ຖ້າເຈົ້າສາມາດຮັກສາຄວາມລັບໄດ້, ຂ້ອຍກໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້.

548
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:45,800
[VINCENT]
Let's shake on it.
ມາສັ່ນສະເທືອນມັນ.

549
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:48,300
[VINCENT]
Mum's the word.
ແມ່ແມ່ນຄໍາເວົ້າ.

550
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:53,350
[VINCENT]
If you'll excuse me, I gotta go home and have a heart attack.
ຖ້າເຈົ້າຂໍໂທດຂ້ອຍ, ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງກັບບ້ານແລະມີການໂຈມຕີຫົວໃຈ.

551
00:34:53,850 --> 00:34:57,000
[MIA]
You still wanna hear my "FOX FORCE FIVE" joke?
ເຈົ້າຍັງຢາກໄດ້ຍິນຢອກຊື່ໆຂອງຂ້ອຍວ່າ"Fox Force Five" ບໍ?

552
00:34:57,500 --> 00:35:01,700
[VINCENT]
Sure, but I think I'm still a little too petrified to laugh.
ແນ່ນອນ, ແຕ່ຂ້ອຍຄິດວ່າຂ້ອຍຍັງຢ້ານກົວເກີນໄປທີ່ຈະມ່ວນຊື່ນ.

553
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:08,200
[MIA]
Uh-huh. You won't laugh because it's not funny. But if you still wanna hear it, I'll tell it.
ອູຮູ. ເຈົ້າຈະບໍ່ມ່ວນເພາະວ່າມັນບໍ່ມ່ວນຊື່ນ
. ແຕ່ຖ້າເຈົ້າຍັງຢາກຍິນມັນ, ຂ້ອຍຈະບອກມັນ.

554
00:35:08,700 --> 00:35:10,700
[VINCENT]
I can't wait.
ຂ້ອຍລໍຖ້າບໍ່ໄດ້.

555
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:17,200
[MIA]
Three tomatoes are walking down the street, a poppa tomato, a momma tomato, and a little baby tomato. The baby tomato is lagging behind the poppa and momma tomato. The poppa tomato gets mad, goes over to the momma tomato and stamps on him �  � and says: catch up.
ຫມາກ ກ້ວຍສາມໂຕ ກໍາ ລັງຍ່າງຕາມຖະຫນົນຫົນທາງ, ຫມາກກ້ວຍພໍ່, ຫມວກ ຫມາກ ຄ້ວຍແມ່, ແລະ ຫມາກ ເກັດເດັກນ້ອຍນ້ອຍໆ. ຫມາກ ເຄັດເດັກນ້ອຍ
ກໍາ ລັງຊ້າຢູ່ເບື້ອງຫຼັງຫມາກເກັດພໍ່ແລະແມ່. ຫມັກ ເຄັດແມ່ໂຊກຮ້າຍ, ໄປຫາຫມາກ ເກີດແມ່ແລະ stamp ກ່ຽວກັບລາວແລະເວົ້າວ່າ: ຕິດຕາມ.

556
00:35:17,700 --> 00:35:19,700
[MIA]
See ya 'round, Vince.
ພົບກັນຢູ່ອ້ອມຂ້າງ, ວິນສ໌.

557
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:26,200
[CLOSEUP � VINCENT]
After Mia walks inside. Vincent continues to look at where she was. He brings his hands to his lips and blows her a kiss. Then exits FRAME leaving it empty. WE HEAR his Malibu START UP and DRIVE AWAY.
ຫຼັງຈາກມິຍຍ່າງເຂົ້າໄປໃນ. ວິນເຊັນສ໌ສືບຕໍ່ເບິ່ງບ່ອນທີ່ນາງຢູ່. ລາວເອົາມືໃສ່ປາກຂອງລາວແລະພັດໃຫ້ນາງຈູບ
. ຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນອອກຈາກກອບປ່ອຍມັນເປົ່າ. ພວກເຮົາໄດ້ຍິນມາລີບູຂອງລາວເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແລະຂັບລົດໄປ.

558
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:32,700
[FADE TO BLACK]
FADE UP On the cartoon "SPEED RACER."  Speed is giving a detailed description of all the features on his race car "The Mac-5," which he does at the beginning of every episode.
ຄວາມໄວ ກໍາ ລັງໃຫ້ ຄໍາ ອະທິບາຍຢ່າງລະອຽດກ່ຽວກັບຄຸນລັກສະນະທັງ ຫມົດ
ໃນລົດແຂ່ງຂັນຂອງລາວ" Mac-5," ເຊິ່ງລາວເຮັດໃນຕອນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຂອງທຸກໆບົດເລື່ອງ.

559
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:35,200
[WOMAN'S VOICE]
Butch.
ບຸດຊ໌.

560
00:35:35,700 --> 00:35:41,700
[MOTHER]
Butch, stop watching TV a second. We got a special visitor. Now do you remember when I told you your daddy dies in a P.O.W. camp?
ບຸດຊ໌, ຢຸດເບິ່ງໂທລະພາບຊົ່ວຄາວຫນຶ່ງ. ພວກເຮົາມີແຂກພິເສດ.
ດຽວນີ້ເຈົ້າຈື່ບໍ່ວ່າຂ້ອຍບອກເຈົ້າວ່າພໍ່ເຈົ້າຕາຍໃນຄ້າຍ POW ບໍ?

561
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:44,200
[BUTCH]
Uh-huh.
ໂອ້.

562
00:35:44,700 --> 00:35:49,600
[MOTHER]
Well this here is Capt. Koons. He was in the P.O.W. camp with Daddy.
ດີນີ້ແມ່ນຄັບປິນ ຄູນສ໌. ລາວຢູ່ໃນຄ້າຍ POW ກັບພໍ່.

563
00:35:50,100 --> 00:35:56,100
[CAPT. KOONS]
Hello, little man. Boy I sure heard a bunch about you. See, I was a good friend of your Daddy's. We were in that Hanoi pit of hell over five years together.  Hopefully, you'll never have to experience this yourself, but when two men are in a situation like me and your Daddy were, for as long as we were, you take on certain responsibilities of the other. If it had been me who had not made it, Major Coolidge would be talkin' right now to my son Jim. But the way it worked out is I'm talkin' to you, Butch. I got somethin' for ya.
ສະບາຍດີ, ຜູ້ຊາຍນ້ອຍ. ເດັກຊາຍຂ້ອຍແນ່ໃຈວ່າໄດ້ຍິນຫຼາຍຢ່າງກ່ຽວກັບເຈົ້າ. ເບິ່ງ, ຂ້ອຍເປັນເພື່ອນທີ່ດີຂອງພໍ່ເຈົ້າ. ພວກເຮົາຢູ່ໃນຮູອານາໄມຮານໂຮຍນັ້ນຫຼາຍກວ່າຫ້າປີຮ່ວມກັນ. ຫວັງວ່າ, ເຈົ້າຈະບໍ່ຕ້ອງປະສົບກັບສິ່ງນີ້ເອງ
, ແຕ່ເມື່ອຜູ້ຊາຍສອງຄົນຢູ່ໃນສະຖານະການຄືກັບຂ້ອຍແລະພໍ່ເຈົ້າ, ຕະຫຼອດທີ່ພວກເຮົາເປັນ, ເຈົ້າຮັບຜິດຊອບບາງສ່ວນຂອງຄົນອື່ນ. ຖ້າມັນແມ່ນຂ້ອຍທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ເຮັດມັນ, ນາຍພົນຄູລີຈ໌ຈະເວົ້າໃນເວລານີ້ກັບລູກຊາຍຂອງຂ້ອຍຈ

564
00:35:56,600 --> 00:36:02,600
[CAPT. KOONS]
This watch I got here was first purchased by your great-granddaddy. It was bought during the First World War in a little general store in Knoxville, Tennessee. It was bought by private Doughboy Ernie Coolidge the day he set sail for Paris. It was your great-granddaddy's war watch, made by the first company to ever make wrist watches. You see, up until then, people just carried pocket watches. Your great-granddaddy wore that watch every day he was in the war. Then when he had done his duty, he went home to your great- grandmother, took the watch off his wrist and put it in an ol' coffee can. And in that can it stayed 'til your grandfather Dane Coolidge was called upon by his country to go overseas and fight the Germans once again. This time they called it World War Two. Your great-granddaddy gave it to your granddad for good luck. Unfortunately, Dane's luck wasn't as good as his old man's. Your granddad was a Marine and he was killed with all the other Marines at the battle of Wake Island. Your granddad was facing death and he knew it. None of those boys had any illusions about ever leavin' that island alive. So three days before the Japanese took the island, your 22-year old grandfather asked a gunner on an Air Force transport named Winocki, a man he had never met before in his life, to deliver to his infant son, who he had never seen in the flesh, his gold watch. Three days later, your grandfather was dead. But Winocki kept his word. After the war was over, he paid a visit to your grandmother, delivering to your infant father, his Dad's gold watch. This watch. This watch was on your Daddy's wrist when he was shot down over Hanoi. He was captured and put in a Vietnamese prison camp. Now he knew if the gooks ever saw the watch it'd be confiscated. The way your Daddy looked at it, that watch was your birthright. And he'd be damned if and slopeheads were gonna put their greasy yella hands on his boy's birthright. So he hid it in the one place he knew he could hide somethin'. His ass. Five long years, he wore this watch up his ass. Then when he died of dysentery, he gave me the watch. I hid with uncomfortable hunk of metal up my ass for two years. Then, after seven years, I was sent home to my family. And now, little man, I give the watch to you.
